; 02-use.kurt

; To reason about anything beyond `true` we need axioms: formulas we simply
; declare to hold, without proof.  The keyword `use` adds such a formula to
; the theory.

bool A

use A                  ; from now on `A` is an axiom
A                       ; ...and so it can be checked

; `use` accepts an optional label describing where the axiom comes from; it
; shows up in the log after "without proof", and later steps cite it by name:

bool B
use B  "our-second-axiom"
B

; `use` with no argument lists every axiom used so far, level by level -- try
; it:

use
